CM Gull
CM
CM W7AY Gull
CM 
CM This is a 1.5 wavelength Vee Beam that has an extra bend on it on each arm of the Vee (which can be
CM made from an extra piece of rope).
CM 
CM It can also be viewed as a piecewise linear version of one element of a Landstorfer-Sacher beam.
CM 
CM It has about 0.8 dB better directivity than a Vee beam of the same length, and has about 0.6 dB forward //	gain than the equivalent Vee Beam while having approximately the same 3 dB beamwidth.
CM
CE
SY height=12
SY d=1in
GW 1,3,0,-d,height,0,d,height,awg14
! 0.75 wavelength nominal
SY y=16.03
SY dt=rho*y
SY dy=dt*sin(theta0)
SY dx=dt*cos(theta0)
GW 2,13,0,-d,height,dx,-dy,height,awg14
GW 3,13,0,d,height,dx,dy,height,awg14
SY dt=(1.0-rho)*y
SY dy1=dy+dt*sin(theta1)
SY dx1=dx+dt*cos(theta1)
GW 4,13,dx,-dy,height,dx1,-dy1,height,awg14
GW 5,13,dx,dy,height,dx1,dy1,height,awg14
GE 0
EX 0,1,2,0,1,0
GN 2,0,0,0,13,0.005
FR 0,1,0,0,14,0
RP 0,37,73,1000,0,0,5,5
EN
